    {
      "id": "4BFgi1S-qdQouFWe_o6GL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 239.95423604521045,
      "y": 2238.2606716862692,
      "width": 945.099365234375,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2u",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1565965644,
      "version": 517,
      "versionNonce": 1970273140,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786558897895,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2. Embeddings:\n   - Numerical vector representation of text that used for semantic relationship b/w content.\n   - Bcz keywords search alone may fail as different word has similar meaning.\n\n3. Vector DB:\n   - It stores the embeddings and provide the efficient similarity search to retrieve semantically.\n   - Examples: pgvector, pinecone, Miluvs\n   - Choice depends on scale, filtering requirements, operational complexity, workloads.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2. Embeddings:\n   - Numerical vector representation of text that used for semantic relationship b/w content.\n   - Bcz keywords search alone may fail as different word has similar meaning.\n\n3. Vector DB:\n   - It stores the embeddings and provide the efficient similarity search to retrieve semantically.\n   - Examples: pgvector, pinecone, Miluvs\n   - Choice depends on scale, filtering requirements, operational complexity, workloads.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "kzBnyty35xtj8xZPc6lYX",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 240.40168032103614,
      "y": 2454.417436656713,
      "width": 1025.599365234375,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2v",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1321164748,
      "version": 399,
      "versionNonce": 492832204,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786633126793,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "4. Chunking:\n    - the process of splitting large documents into smaller chunks before embeddings and indexing them\n    - each chunk embedded separately and retrieval needs to identify small releavant piece of info\n    - Document\n           ↓\n        Chunk 1\n        Chunk 2\n        Chunk 3\n        ...\n        Chunk N\n    - Common chunking strategies:\n        1. Fixed-size chunking: Split text every N tokens or characters.\n        2. Fixed-size with overlap (most common): Adjacent chunks share some content. (overlap: 10-20%)\n            Example:  Chunk 1: Tokens 1–500\n                        Chunk 2: Tokens 401–900\n                        Chunk 3: Tokens 801–1300\n        3. Sentence/paragraph-based chunking: Split by sentences/para while keeping a target chunk size.\n        4. Semantic chunking: Instead of splitting by size, split where the topic changes.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "4. Chunking:\n    - the process of splitting large documents into smaller chunks before embeddings and indexing them\n    - each chunk embedded separately and retrieval needs to identify small releavant piece of info\n    - Document\n           ↓\n        Chunk 1\n        Chunk 2\n        Chunk 3\n        ...\n        Chunk N\n    - Common chunking strategies:\n        1. Fixed-size chunking: Split text every N tokens or characters.\n        2. Fixed-size with overlap (most common): Adjacent chunks share some content. (overlap: 10-20%)\n            Example:  Chunk 1: Tokens 1–500\n                        Chunk 2: Tokens 401–900\n                        Chunk 3: Tokens 801–1300\n        3. Sentence/paragraph-based chunking: Split by sentences/para while keeping a target chunk size.\n        4. Semantic chunking: Instead of splitting by size, split where the topic changes.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "W7_5L7Cwwfu3CF-o-fj2a",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 262.96030940514527,
      "y": 2937.461285155096,
      "width": 1486.21875,
      "height": 1200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2w",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1900888436,
      "version": 1751,
      "versionNonce": 94801908,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786643689478,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "5. Retrieval: a system finds the most relevant chunks of info from knowledge base for user's question.\n    - User asks a question → RAG searches its stored knowledge → finds relevant chunks → gives those chunks to the LLM.\n    - Retrieval system calculates the similarity b/w question embeddings and chunk embeddings and return most relevant ones. -- Vector/Semantic search\n    - Common retrieval strategies:\n        1. (Dense) Basic vector retrieval: Query -> Embeddings -> Vector search -> Top-K chunks -> LLM\n        2. (Sparse) Keyword / BM-25 retrieval: Instead of semantic search , search for matching words. Good for error codes search.\n        3. Hybrid retrieval: Combine vector search + Keyword search ; Good for Prod RAG, Enterprise RAG.\n        4. Top-K retrieval: Retrieve the top-k most relevant chunks; if k=small - will miss important info; if k=huge - context irrelevant, high token usage\n        5. Metadata filtering: Before or during retrieval, filter docs using metadata then do vector search on filtered docs; Enterprise RAG.\n        6. Retrieval + reranking: Instead of directly using first-K vector results:\n                        Query\n                         ↓\n                        Vector search\n                         ↓\n                        Top 20 chunks\n                         ↓\n                        Reranker\n                         ↓\n                        Best 5 chunks\n                         ↓\n                        LLM\n                - Reranker performs more expensive relevance & precision comparison b/w chunks.\n        7. Multi-query retrieval: Instead of one query, generate similar queries and send to Retrieval\n        8. Query Rewrite: Improve the user query ; useful for Conversational RAG\n        9. Hierarchal retrieval: Search at multiple levels\n                Find relevant document\n                        ↓\n                Find relevant section\n                        ↓\n                Find relevant paragraphs\n                        ↓\n                Give to LLM\n        10. Agentic/Iterative retrieval: LLM decides what info it needs and perform multiple searches.\n                    User question\n                         ↓\n                        LLM\n                         ↓\n                    Search #1\n                         ↓\n                    Read results\n                         ↓\n                    Need more information?\n                         ↓\n                    Search #2\n                         ↓\n                    Read results\n                         ↓\n                    Final answer",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "5. Retrieval: a system finds the most relevant chunks of info from knowledge base for user's question.\n    - User asks a question → RAG searches its stored knowledge → finds relevant chunks → gives those chunks to the LLM.\n    - Retrieval system calculates the similarity b/w question embeddings and chunk embeddings and return most relevant ones. -- Vector/Semantic search\n    - Common retrieval strategies:\n        1. (Dense) Basic vector retrieval: Query -> Embeddings -> Vector search -> Top-K chunks -> LLM\n        2. (Sparse) Keyword / BM-25 retrieval: Instead of semantic search , search for matching words. Good for error codes search.\n        3. Hybrid retrieval: Combine vector search + Keyword search ; Good for Prod RAG, Enterprise RAG.\n        4. Top-K retrieval: Retrieve the top-k most relevant chunks; if k=small - will miss important info; if k=huge - context irrelevant, high token usage\n        5. Metadata filtering: Before or during retrieval, filter docs using metadata then do vector search on filtered docs; Enterprise RAG.\n        6. Retrieval + reranking: Instead of directly using first-K vector results:\n                        Query\n                         ↓\n                        Vector search\n                         ↓\n                        Top 20 chunks\n                         ↓\n                        Reranker\n                         ↓\n                        Best 5 chunks\n                         ↓\n                        LLM\n                - Reranker performs more expensive relevance & precision comparison b/w chunks.\n        7. Multi-query retrieval: Instead of one query, generate similar queries and send to Retrieval\n        8. Query Rewrite: Improve the user query ; useful for Conversational RAG\n        9. Hierarchal retrieval: Search at multiple levels\n                Find relevant document\n                        ↓\n                Find relevant section\n                        ↓\n                Find relevant paragraphs\n                        ↓\n                Give to LLM\n        10. Agentic/Iterative retrieval: LLM decides what info it needs and perform multiple searches.\n                    User question\n                         ↓\n                        LLM\n                         ↓\n                    Search #1\n                         ↓\n                    Read results\n                         ↓\n                    Need more information?\n                         ↓\n                    Search #2\n                         ↓\n                    Read results\n                         ↓\n                    Final answer",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
