    {
      "id": "GyRB8YOuZoeRD8PZo2l54",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3580.3222809243293,
      "y": 2286.1163488845377,
      "width": 1056.9793701171875,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4g",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1457281484,
      "version": 816,
      "versionNonce": 186755404,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786775602668,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "       - Tools permissions:  Add a permissions to tool calls to have unrestricted access to everything.\n            search_documents() → allowed\n            get_order()        → allowed\n            send_email()       → requires confirmation\n            delete_account()   → prohibited\n            transfer_money()   → prohibited\n          - Never trust LLM decision to call a tool as authorization to perform action.\n        - Human-in-the-loop: For high-risk actions, requires human input\n               - useful for - Financial transactions, Account deletion, Legal decisions, High-value refunds\n        - PII protection: PII - Personally identifiable information\n                User input\n                    ↓\n                PII detection\n                    ↓\n                Mask / redact / allow\n                    ↓\n                LLM\n            Example: you should redact data depends on your application's requirements and privacy policies\n                My phone number is [PHONE]\n                and my email is [EMAIL].\n    - Guardrails help detect or prevent some failure modes, but they don't magically make the model truthful.\n    - A guardrail can be actual application logic not just prompt instruction\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "       - Tools permissions:  Add a permissions to tool calls to have unrestricted access to everything.\n            search_documents() → allowed\n            get_order()        → allowed\n            send_email()       → requires confirmation\n            delete_account()   → prohibited\n            transfer_money()   → prohibited\n          - Never trust LLM decision to call a tool as authorization to perform action.\n        - Human-in-the-loop: For high-risk actions, requires human input\n               - useful for - Financial transactions, Account deletion, Legal decisions, High-value refunds\n        - PII protection: PII - Personally identifiable information\n                User input\n                    ↓\n                PII detection\n                    ↓\n                Mask / redact / allow\n                    ↓\n                LLM\n            Example: you should redact data depends on your application's requirements and privacy policies\n                My phone number is [PHONE]\n                and my email is [EMAIL].\n    - Guardrails help detect or prevent some failure modes, but they don't magically make the model truthful.\n    - A guardrail can be actual application logic not just prompt instruction\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
