    },
    {
      "id": "R_BsJDOt_hSchpr4OVCgZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3568.080084359224,
      "y": 2935.400433654067,
      "width": 1391.0391845703125,
      "height": 1350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5W",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1631270516,
      "version": 1307,
      "versionNonce": 732005364,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786782803186,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "6. Evaluation:\n    - Validation of answer from LLM\n    - Evaluate whole pipeline not just LLM.\n    1. Retrieval evaluation:\n        - did retireval finds the correct document?\n        - metrics: \n            - Recall@K: of all relevant information trhat exists, how much did retrieval find? = Did I find the relevant stuff?\n            - Precision@K: of what i retrieved , how much are actually relevant? = How much of what I found is relevant?\n    2. Reranking evaluation:\n        - we can evaluate the reranker correctly moves relevant chunks to top.\n        - Did the relevant result appear near the top?\n        - Metrics: MRR (Mean Reciprocal Rank) and NDCG\n    3. Generation evaluation:\n        - is the generated answer good?\n        - Metrics: \n            - Correctness: Does the answer actually answer the question correctly?\n            - Relevance: Is the answer relevant to the user's question?\n            - Faithfulness / Groundedness: Is the answer supported by the retrieved context?\n    4. LLM-as-a-judge:\n        - LLM as a evaluator\n        - Question\n          Context\n          Generated answer\n              ↓\n          Judge LLM\n              ↓\n            Score\n    5. Human evaluation: Humans can identify problems that automated miss.\n    6. Evaluation dataset: Create a output dataset and if RAG then add source also and every system update runs the test.\n    7. LLM regression test: \n            Code change\n                ↓\n            Run evaluation dataset\n                ↓\n            Compare metrics\n                ↓\n            Pass?\n             ┌──┴──┐\n            Yes            No\n             ↓              ↓\n            Deploy     Investigate\n    8. Production evaluation: Monitor real usage : retrieval latency, LLM latency, token usage, error rates, retrieval failure, tool calling failures, \n            users feedback, answer quality.\n\n                RAG QUALITY\n                      │\n       ┌─────┼───────┐\n       ↓              ↓                  ↓\n   Retrieval     Generation      Safety\n       │              │               │\n   Recall@K       Correctness   Violations\n   Precision@K    Relevance     PII\n   MRR            Faithfulness  Injection\n   NDCG           Grounding     Policy",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "6. Evaluation:\n    - Validation of answer from LLM\n    - Evaluate whole pipeline not just LLM.\n    1. Retrieval evaluation:\n        - did retireval finds the correct document?\n        - metrics: \n            - Recall@K: of all relevant information trhat exists, how much did retrieval find? = Did I find the relevant stuff?\n            - Precision@K: of what i retrieved , how much are actually relevant? = How much of what I found is relevant?\n    2. Reranking evaluation:\n        - we can evaluate the reranker correctly moves relevant chunks to top.\n        - Did the relevant result appear near the top?\n        - Metrics: MRR (Mean Reciprocal Rank) and NDCG\n    3. Generation evaluation:\n        - is the generated answer good?\n        - Metrics: \n            - Correctness: Does the answer actually answer the question correctly?\n            - Relevance: Is the answer relevant to the user's question?\n            - Faithfulness / Groundedness: Is the answer supported by the retrieved context?\n    4. LLM-as-a-judge:\n        - LLM as a evaluator\n        - Question\n          Context\n          Generated answer\n              ↓\n          Judge LLM\n              ↓\n            Score\n    5. Human evaluation: Humans can identify problems that automated miss.\n    6. Evaluation dataset: Create a output dataset and if RAG then add source also and every system update runs the test.\n    7. LLM regression test: \n            Code change\n                ↓\n            Run evaluation dataset\n                ↓\n            Compare metrics\n                ↓\n            Pass?\n             ┌──┴──┐\n            Yes            No\n             ↓              ↓\n            Deploy     Investigate\n    8. Production evaluation: Monitor real usage : retrieval latency, LLM latency, token usage, error rates, retrieval failure, tool calling failures, \n            users feedback, answer quality.\n\n                RAG QUALITY\n                      │\n       ┌─────┼───────┐\n       ↓              ↓                  ↓\n   Retrieval     Generation      Safety\n       │              │               │\n   Recall@K       Correctness   Violations\n   Precision@K    Relevance     PII\n   MRR            Faithfulness  Injection\n   NDCG           Grounding     Policy",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
